Desktop-notification support for st.

Three notification paths, all routed through notify-send:

  1. Bell-on-unfocus  — when st receives BEL (\a) while the window is
     unfocused, fire notify-send. Controlled by `bellnotify` in config.h.
     Catches anything that already rings the terminal bell (Claude Code's
     idle/waiting indicator, irc clients, shell PROMPT_COMMAND, etc.) with
     zero config on the source side.

  2. OSC 9  (iTerm2-style)  — `\033]9;Message\007`
     Fires unconditionally with title="st" and the supplied body.

  3. OSC 777 (urxvt-style)  — `\033]777;notify;Title;Body\007`
     Fires unconditionally with separate title and body.

OSC paths bypass `bellnotify` because they are explicit requests from a
program — not the implicit "something rang the bell" signal.

For OSC traversal through tmux, the outer tmux needs:
    set -g allow-passthrough on

Implementation:

* win.h
  - declare void xnotify(const char *, const char *);

* config.def.h / config.h
  - bellnotify   (int, default 1)
  - notifycmd    (str, default "notify-send")
  - notifyappname (str, default "st" — used as -a APPNAME)

* x.c
  - #include <sys/wait.h>
  - xnotify(title, body): double-fork + execlp notify-send so the child
    reparents to init (no zombies, no SIGCHLD interaction with the shell).
    Passes "-a APPNAME -i utilities-terminal TITLE BODY".
  - xbell(): when window is unfocused and bellnotify is set, also call
    xnotify(appname, "Bell"). Pre-existing XkbBell behavior unchanged.

* st.c
  - strhandle() OSC switch: add case 9 (iTerm) and case 777 (urxvt,
    "notify" subcommand only).
